WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:06.040
I think now for Rapsida, it's really just a story of step-by-step continuing to drive

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.680
up the access environment.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:12.880
I mean, we see strong demand, very strong demand in the dermatology segment.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.700
We're working on building stronger demand as well in the allergy segment.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.180
In general, once physicians start using the medicine and they get the feedback from the

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.220
patients that they're seeing disease.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.820
And so, you know, I think that there's a lot of improvement within, within hours and certainly

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.820
within a week that gives a very compelling case to continued use.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.240
But we're trying to stay really disciplined on the gross to net here.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:43.040
We just believe that if we play the long run out here, remibrutinib has the potential

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.200
to be used in a broad range of indications, as you all well know, and any points we give

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.640
now, we won't be able to get back in the future.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.320
And so we're just being very thoughtful.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.440
So I think the access will improve.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.160
We'll improve sequentially over the course of this year.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.180
But that will ultimately set us up, I think, for a strong 2027 and then a strong longer

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.180
term outlook for remibrutinib in the future.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.200
Thank you.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.340
Thank you.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.740
I will now hand the call back to you, Vas.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.240
Absolutely.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.820
And I just wanted to come back to Richard Vosser's question.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:22.620
We can confirm that the PCSK9 use was just modestly increased versus the 11% from the

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.740
baseline population.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.060
So.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.680
That is not a significant factor we would expect in the studies.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.680
But thanks for that question, Richard.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.680
So thanks, everyone, for joining today's conference call.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.000
So we'll look forward to keeping you up to speed as we have the readouts over the coming

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.200
months and, of course, catching up with you in various settings in the meantime.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.880
And we look forward to a strong second half and wish you all a great summer break as well.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:45.400
Thank you.

